---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const faqSchema = {
 "@context": "https://schema.org",
 "@type": "FAQPage",
 "mainEntity": [
    {'@type': 'Question', 'name': "Does HSTS affect SEO?", "acceptedAnswer": { '@type': 'Answer', "text": "Google indexes HTTPS preferentially; HSTS signals and enforces commitment. Redirects remain necessary for HTTP requests." } },
    {'@type': 'Question', 'name': "Can I exclude one subdomain?", "acceptedAnswer": { '@type': 'Answer', "text": "Not with includeSubDomains active: that flag covers everything. Plan subdomains before enabling it." } },
    {'@type': 'Question', 'name': "What is HSTS for cookies?", "acceptedAnswer": { '@type': 'Answer', "text": "The same idea applies to cookies (Secure flag): HSTS complements it by forcing the transport itself." } },
    {'@type': 'Question', 'name': "I set max-age=0 to disable HSTS. Did it work?", "acceptedAnswer": { '@type': 'Answer', "text": "For browsers that saw the header: yes, max-age=0 expires the policy. Preload list removal is separate and slow." } },
    {'@type': 'Question', 'name': "Does my CDN handle HSTS?", "acceptedAnswer": { '@type': 'Answer', "text": "Cloudflare and others can inject it; check the response header to confirm what is actually being sent." } }
  ]
}
---
<BaseLayout
  title="HSTS: HTTP Strict Transport Security"
  description="HSTS explained: how the Strict-Transport-Security header forces HTTPS permanently, protects against downgrade attacks, and the risks of getting it wrong."
  schema={[faqSchema]}
 breadcrumb={[["Home", "/"], ["SSL/TLS Guides", "/ssl-tls/"], ["HSTS"]]}>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/ssl-tls/" class="hover:text-accent">SSL/TLS Guides</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">HSTS</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">HSTS: HTTP Strict Transport Security</h1>
    <div class="pd-answer" data-vs="answer">
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">HSTS is one response header that changes your security posture permanently: once a browser sees it for your domain, it refuses to connect over HTTP at all, eliminating downgrade attacks and the "type http:// manually" gap.</p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">HSTS attributes</h2>
    <section class="not-prose my-4" aria-label="Reference table">
      <div class="glass rounded-2xl p-5 shadow-lg sm:p-7 overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="pdns-table" style="width:100%">
          <thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">max-age</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Enforcement duration</td></tr><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">includeSubDomains</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">All subdomains</td></tr><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">preload</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Preload list</td></tr></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>
<nav class="pd-toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-accent">On this page</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="#the-header">The header</a></li>
        <li><a href="#what-hsts-stops">What HSTS stops</a></li>
        <li><a href="#the-deployment-ritual">The deployment ritual</a></li>
        <li><a href="#frequently-asked-questions">Frequently asked questions</a></li>
        <li><a href="#related">Related</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>
    <div class="rich-text mt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink" id="the-header">The header</h2>
      <pre class="rounded-lg border border-line bg-panel-2 p-4 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-accent-soft">Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload</pre><ul class="list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 mt-3"><li><strong class="text-ink">max-age:</strong> how long the browser remembers (seconds). Start small (300) while testing, raise to 31536000 once confident.</li><li><strong class="text-ink">includeSubDomains:</strong> forces HTTPS on every subdomain, including ones you add later.</li><li><strong class="text-ink">preload:</strong> permission to embed you in the browser-built-in list; the strongest form, and effectively irreversible.</li></ul>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink" id="what-hsts-stops">What HSTS stops</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li>SSL-stripping attacks: the man-in-the-middle trick of downgrading to HTTP.</li><li>Users typing http:// or clicking http links on the first visit after the policy is cached.</li><li>Warnings suppressed: browsers fail hard instead of offering an override.</li></ul>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink" id="the-deployment-ritual">The deployment ritual</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li>Confirm HTTPS works on the apex, www, and every subdomain.</li><li>Send max-age=300 for a week; watch for breakage.</li><li>Raise to max-age=86400, then 31536000.</li><li>Only then add includeSubDomains, and preload last, after submitting to hstspreload.org.</li></ol><p>Rolling back preload is genuinely slow (list removal takes weeks through browser releases). Never preload a domain whose subdomains you do not fully control.</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink" id="frequently-asked-questions">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Does HSTS affect SEO?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Google indexes HTTPS preferentially; HSTS signals and enforces commitment. Redirects remain necessary for HTTP requests.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Can I exclude one subdomain?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Not with includeSubDomains active: that flag covers everything. Plan subdomains before enabling it.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What is HSTS for cookies?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">The same idea applies to cookies (Secure flag): HSTS complements it by forcing the transport itself.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">I set max-age=0 to disable HSTS. Did it work?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">For browsers that saw the header: yes, max-age=0 expires the policy. Preload list removal is separate and slow.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Does my CDN handle HSTS?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Cloudflare and others can inject it; check the response header to confirm what is actually being sent.</p></details></div>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink" id="related">Related</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 grid gap-2"><li><a href="/ssl-tls/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">SSL/TLS hub →</a></li><li><a href="/mixed-content-fix/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">Mixed content fixes →</a></li><li><a href="/tls-versions-explained/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">TLS versions →</a></li></ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
